  "category": "Graph",
  "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/graph-valid-tree/",
  "statement": "Given an integer n representing the number of nodes in a graph and a list of edges, determine whether the given edges form a valid tree.\n\nA valid tree must satisfy two conditions:\n1. It is a connected graph (all nodes are reachable from any node)\n2. It contains no cycles (it is acyclic)\n\nEquivalently, a tree with n nodes has exactly n-1 edges and is fully connected.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= n <= 10^4",
    "0 <= edges.length <= 10^4",
    "edges[i].length == 2",
    "0 <= edges[i][0], edges[i][1] < n",
    "edges[i][0] != edges[i][1]"
  ],
  "signature": {
    "className": "Solution",
    "methodName": "validTree",
    "params": [
      {
